; An effect operation performed with no handler in dynamic extent is a
; trap, not a garbage dispatch: the program exits 71 (the allocators'
; out-of-memory path owns 70) before the operation could "return" a
; value nothing produced. The handle around `covered` proves the trap
; really is about dynamic extent: the same operation, one line earlier,
; dispatched fine and printed nothing.
;
; The tag is this fixture's subject written down. AX3053 reports an
; operation reaching `main` with no handler, and it reports this one -
; correctly, since the program does exit 71. `;@axiom:unhandled(trap)`
; is how a program says the trap is what it wants, which is what this
; file has always meant.
;@axiom:unhandled(trap)
(effect Console
  (log :: (-> String Int)))

(:: covered (-> Int Int))

(fn (covered n)
  (handle (log "handled fine") (Console) (lambda (s) 0))
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  {
    (covered 1)
    (log "nobody home")
  }
)
